---
import CalculatorLayout from '../../layouts/CalculatorLayout.astro';
---

<CalculatorLayout
  title="Exponential Form Calculator – Convert Numbers, Logs & Exponents"
  description="Convert whole numbers to exponential form via prime factorization, and easily convert between logarithmic and exponential expressions online."
  category="Math"
  calculatorName="Exponential Form Calculator"
  slug="exponential-form-calculator"
  keywords={[
    'exponential form calculator',
    'exponential form',
    'exponential notation calculator',
    'log to exponential form',
    'exponential to logarithmic form',
    'logarithm to exponential',
    'exponential to log calculator',
    'write numbers in exponential form',
    'exponential form of a number',
    'prime factorization exponential form'
  ]}
>
  <div class="space-y-6">

    <!-- MODE SELECTOR TABS -->
    <div class="rounded-2xl border border-slate-200/90 bg-white p-2.5 shadow-2xs dark:border-slate-800 dark:bg-slate-900">
      <div class="flex items-center gap-1.5 overflow-x-auto pb-1 text-xs font-semibold scrollbar-thin">
        <button
          type="button"
          class="btn-exp-tab active shrink-0 rounded-lg bg-blue-600 px-3 py-2 font-bold text-white shadow-xs cursor-pointer transition"
          data-tab="tab-whole"
          id="tab-btn-whole"
        >
          🔢 Whole Number → Exponential Form
        </button>
        <button
          type="button"
          class="btn-exp-tab shrink-0 rounded-lg border border-slate-300 bg-white px-3 py-2 font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:bg-slate-100 dark:border-slate-700 dark:bg-slate-800 dark:text-slate-200 cursor-pointer transition"
          data-tab="tab-log-to-exp"
          id="tab-btn-log-to-exp"
        >
          📐 Logarithmic → Exponential Form
        </button>
        <button
          type="button"
          class="btn-exp-tab shrink-0 rounded-lg border border-slate-300 bg-white px-3 py-2 font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:bg-slate-100 dark:border-slate-700 dark:bg-slate-800 dark:text-slate-200 cursor-pointer transition"
          data-tab="tab-exp-to-log"
          id="tab-btn-exp-to-log"
        >
          ⚡ Exponential → Logarithmic Form
        </button>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- QUICK EXAMPLE PRESETS BAR -->
    <div class="rounded-2xl border border-slate-200/90 bg-white p-3.5 shadow-2xs dark:border-slate-800 dark:bg-slate-900">
      <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-1.5 text-xs">
        <span class="font-bold text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400 mr-1 flex items-center gap-1">
          <span>⚡</span> Quick Presets:
        </span>
        <button type="button" class="btn-preset rounded-lg border border-slate-300 bg-white px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-blue-500 hover:text-blue-600 dark:border-slate-700 dark:bg-slate-800 dark:text-slate-200 cursor-pointer transition" data-mode="whole" data-val="128">128 ➔ 2⁷</button>
        <button type="button" class="btn-preset rounded-lg border border-slate-300 bg-white px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-blue-500 hover:text-blue-600 dark:border-slate-700 dark:bg-slate-800 dark:text-slate-200 cursor-pointer transition" data-mode="whole" data-val="72">72 ➔ 2³ × 3²</button>
        <button type="button" class="btn-preset rounded-lg border border-slate-300 bg-white px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-blue-500 hover:text-blue-600 dark:border-slate-700 dark:bg-slate-800 dark:text-slate-200 cursor-pointer transition" data-mode="whole" data-val="250">250 ➔ 2 × 5³</button>
        <button type="button" class="btn-preset rounded-lg border border-slate-300 bg-white px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-blue-500 hover:text-blue-600 dark:border-slate-700 dark:bg-slate-800 dark:text-slate-200 cursor-pointer transition" data-mode="whole" data-val="360">360 ➔ 2³ × 3² × 5</button>
        <button type="button" class="btn-preset rounded-lg border border-slate-300 bg-white px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-blue-500 hover:text-blue-600 dark:border-slate-700 dark:bg-slate-800 dark:text-slate-200 cursor-pointer transition" data-mode="log-to-exp" data-base="2" data-arg="8" data-val="3">log₂(8) = 3</button>
        <button type="button" class="btn-preset rounded-lg border border-slate-300 bg-white px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-blue-500 hover:text-blue-600 dark:border-slate-700 dark:bg-slate-800 dark:text-slate-200 cursor-pointer transition" data-mode="log-to-exp" data-base="5" data-arg="125" data-val="3">log₅(125) = 3</button>
        <button type="button" class="btn-preset rounded-lg border border-slate-300 bg-white px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-blue-500 hover:text-blue-600 dark:border-slate-700 dark:bg-slate-800 dark:text-slate-200 cursor-pointer transition" data-mode="log-to-exp" data-base="e" data-arg="7.389" data-val="2">ln(7.389) ≈ 2</button>
        <button type="button" class="btn-preset rounded-lg border border-slate-300 bg-white px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-blue-500 hover:text-blue-600 dark:border-slate-700 dark:bg-slate-800 dark:text-slate-200 cursor-pointer transition" data-mode="exp-to-log" data-base="2" data-exp="5" data-res="32">2⁵ = 32</button>
        <button type="button" class="btn-preset rounded-lg border border-slate-300 bg-white px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-blue-500 hover:text-blue-600 dark:border-slate-700 dark:bg-slate-800 dark:text-slate-200 cursor-pointer transition" data-mode="exp-to-log" data-base="3" data-exp="4" data-res="81">3⁴ = 81</button>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- MAIN CALCULATOR CONTAINER -->
    <div class="overflow-hidden rounded-3xl border border-slate-200/90 bg-linear-to-br from-white via-slate-50 to-blue-50/30 p-5 shadow-xl shadow-slate-900/5 dark:border-slate-800 dark:from-slate-950 dark:via-slate-950 dark:to-blue-950/20 sm:p-7">

      <!-- 1. MODE A: WHOLE NUMBER -> EXPONENTIAL FORM -->
      <div id="panel-whole" class="exp-panel space-y-5">
        <div class="border-b border-slate-200/80 pb-3 dark:border-slate-800">
          <h2 class="text-base sm:text-lg font-black tracking-tight text-slate-900 dark:text-white flex items-center gap-2">
            <span>🔢</span> Convert Positive Whole Number to Exponential Form
          </h2>
          <p class="mt-1 text-xs text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400">
            Find the prime factorization of any positive integer and represent repeated factors as powers.
          </p>
        </div>

        <form id="form-whole" class="space-y-4" novalidate onsubmit="return false;">
          <div>
            <label for="input-whole-num" class="block text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300">
              Positive Whole Number
            </label>
            <div class="mt-1.5 flex gap-2">
              <input
                type="text"
                id="input-whole-num"
                value=""
                placeholder="e.g. 250, 128, 360, 72"
                class="w-full rounded-xl border border-slate-300 bg-white p-3 text-base font-bold text-slate-900 shadow-2xs focus:border-blue-600 focus:outline-hidden dark:border-slate-700 dark:bg-slate-900 dark:text-white"
                autocomplete="off"
              />
            </div>
            <p class="mt-1 text-[11px] text-slate-500 dark:text-slate-400">
              Enter any positive integer (&gt; 0). Decimals and negative numbers are not accepted for prime factorization.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="flex items-center gap-2 pt-1">
            <button
              type="submit"
              id="btn-calc-whole"
              class="flex-1 rounded-xl bg-blue-600 hover:bg-blue-700 px-6 py-3 text-sm font-extrabold text-white shadow-lg shadow-blue-600/25 transition active:scale-[0.98] cursor-pointer"
            >
              Convert to Exponential Form →
            </button>
            <button
              type="button"
              id="btn-clear-whole"
              class="rounded-xl border border-slate-300 bg-white px-4 py-3 text-sm font-bold text-slate-700 hover:bg-slate-100 dark:border-slate-700 dark:bg-slate-800 dark:text-slate-200 transition cursor-pointer"
            >
              Clear
            </button>
          </div>

          <p id="err-whole" class="hidden rounded-xl border border-red-200 bg-red-50 p-3 text-xs font-semibold text-red-700 dark:border-red-900/60 dark:bg-red-950/30 dark:text-red-300" role="alert" aria-live="polite"></p>

          <!-- Result Box -->
          <div id="res-whole-card" class="hidden space-y-4 rounded-3xl border border-blue-200 bg-white p-5 dark:border-blue-900/60 dark:bg-slate-900">
            <div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row sm:items-center sm:justify-between gap-3 border-b border-slate-200 pb-4 dark:border-slate-800">
              <div>
                <span class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-blue-700 dark:text-blue-400">Exponential Form</span>
                <div id="res-whole-exp" class="mt-1 text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-black text-blue-600 dark:text-blue-400 font-mono">2 × 5³</div>
              </div>
              <div class="sm:text-right">
                <span id="badge-prime-status" class="inline-flex items-center rounded-full bg-slate-100 px-3 py-1 text-xs font-bold text-slate-800 dark:bg-slate-800 dark:text-slate-200">
                  Composite Number
                </span>
              </div>
            </div>

            <div class="rounded-xl border border-slate-200 bg-slate-50/80 p-3.5 dark:border-slate-800 dark:bg-slate-950">
              <span class="text-xs font-semibold text-slate-500 dark:text-slate-400 block mb-1">Prime Factorization:</span>
              <div id="res-whole-expanded" class="text-sm font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white font-mono">
                250 = 2 × 5 × 5 × 5
              </div>
            </div>

            <details class="group rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 bg-slate-50 p-4 dark:border-slate-800 dark:bg-slate-950" open>
              <summary class="cursor-pointer list-none flex items-center justify-between text-xs font-bold text-slate-800 dark:text-slate-200">
                <span>📝 Step-by-Step Prime Factorization Breakdown</span>
                <span class="text-blue-600 dark:text-blue-400 group-open:rotate-180 transition-transform">▼</span>
              </summary>
              <ol id="res-whole-steps" class="mt-3 space-y-1.5 text-xs text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300 list-decimal list-inside font-mono leading-relaxed"></ol>
            </details>
          </div>
        </form>
      </div>

      <!-- 2. MODE B: LOGARITHMIC -> EXPONENTIAL FORM -->
      <div id="panel-log-to-exp" class="exp-panel hidden space-y-5">
        <div class="border-b border-slate-200/80 pb-3 dark:border-slate-800">
          <h2 class="text-base sm:text-lg font-black tracking-tight text-slate-900 dark:text-white flex items-center gap-2">
            <span>📐</span> Convert Logarithmic Expression to Exponential Form
          </h2>
          <p class="mt-1 text-xs text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400">
            Apply the identity <strong class="font-mono">log_b(c) = a ⟺ bᵃ = c</strong> (or <strong class="font-mono">ln(c) = a ⟺ eᵃ = c</strong>).
          </p>
        </div>

        <form id="form-log" class="space-y-4" novalidate onsubmit="return false;">
          <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-3 gap-4">
            
            <!-- Log Base (b) -->
            <div>
              <div class="flex items-center justify-between">
                <label for="input-log-base" class="block text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300">
                  Base (b)
                </label>
                <button type="button" id="btn-use-e-base" class="text-[11px] font-bold text-blue-600 hover:underline dark:text-blue-400 cursor-pointer">
                  Use Natural e
                </button>
              </div>
              <input
                type="text"
                id="input-log-base"
                value=""
                placeholder="e.g. 2, 10, or e"
                class="mt-1.5 w-full rounded-xl border border-slate-300 bg-white p-3 text-base font-bold text-slate-900 shadow-2xs focus:border-blue-600 focus:outline-hidden dark:border-slate-700 dark:bg-slate-900 dark:text-white"
              />
              <span class="text-[11px] text-slate-500 mt-1 block">b &gt; 0 and b ≠ 1</span>
            </div>

            <!-- Number / Argument (c) -->
            <div>
              <label for="input-log-arg" class="block text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300">
                Number / Argument (c)
              </label>
              <input
                type="number"
                id="input-log-arg"
                value=""
                step="any"
                placeholder="e.g. 8, 125, 15"
                class="mt-1.5 w-full rounded-xl border border-slate-300 bg-white p-3 text-base font-bold text-slate-900 shadow-2xs focus:border-blue-600 focus:outline-hidden dark:border-slate-700 dark:bg-slate-900 dark:text-white"
              />
              <span class="text-[11px] text-slate-500 mt-1 block">c &gt; 0</span>
            </div>

            <!-- Log Value / Exponent (a) -->
            <div>
              <label for="input-log-val" class="block text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300">
                Logarithm Value (a)
              </label>
              <input
                type="number"
                id="input-log-val"
                value=""
                step="any"
                placeholder="Optional (auto-computed)"
                class="mt-1.5 w-full rounded-xl border border-slate-300 bg-white p-3 text-base font-bold text-slate-900 shadow-2xs focus:border-blue-600 focus:outline-hidden dark:border-slate-700 dark:bg-slate-900 dark:text-white"
              />
              <span class="text-[11px] text-slate-500 mt-1 block">Leave empty to compute automatically</span>
            </div>

          </div>

          <div class="flex items-center gap-2 pt-1">
            <button
              type="submit"
              id="btn-calc-log"
              class="flex-1 rounded-xl bg-blue-600 hover:bg-blue-700 px-6 py-3 text-sm font-extrabold text-white shadow-lg shadow-blue-600/25 transition active:scale-[0.98] cursor-pointer"
            >
              Convert to Exponential Form →
            </button>
            <button
              type="button"
              id="btn-clear-log"
              class="rounded-xl border border-slate-300 bg-white px-4 py-3 text-sm font-bold text-slate-700 hover:bg-slate-100 dark:border-slate-700 dark:bg-slate-800 dark:text-slate-200 transition cursor-pointer"
            >
              Clear
            </button>
          </div>

          <p id="err-log" class="hidden rounded-xl border border-red-200 bg-red-50 p-3 text-xs font-semibold text-red-700 dark:border-red-900/60 dark:bg-red-950/30 dark:text-red-300" role="alert" aria-live="polite"></p>

          <!-- Result Card -->
          <div id="res-log-card" class="hidden space-y-4 rounded-3xl border border-blue-200 bg-white p-5 dark:border-blue-900/60 dark:bg-slate-900">
            <div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row sm:items-center sm:justify-between gap-3 border-b border-slate-200 pb-4 dark:border-slate-800">
              <div>
                <span class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-blue-700 dark:text-blue-400">Equivalent Exponential Form</span>
                <div id="res-log-exp" class="mt-1 text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-black text-blue-600 dark:text-blue-400 font-mono">2³ = 8</div>
              </div>
              <div class="sm:text-right">
                <span class="text-xs font-bold text-slate-500 uppercase tracking-wider">Input Logarithm:</span>
                <div id="res-log-in" class="text-sm sm:text-base font-bold text-slate-800 dark:text-slate-200 font-mono">log₂(8) = 3</div>
              </div>
            </div>

            <details class="group rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 bg-slate-50 p-4 dark:border-slate-800 dark:bg-slate-950" open>
              <summary class="cursor-pointer list-none flex items-center justify-between text-xs font-bold text-slate-800 dark:text-slate-200">
                <span>📝 Step-by-Step Conversion Derivation</span>
                <span class="text-blue-600 dark:text-blue-400 group-open:rotate-180 transition-transform">▼</span>
              </summary>
              <ul id="res-log-steps" class="mt-3 space-y-1.5 text-xs text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300 list-disc list-inside font-mono leading-relaxed"></ul>
            </details>
          </div>
        </form>
      </div>

      <!-- 3. MODE C: EXPONENTIAL -> LOGARITHMIC FORM -->
      <div id="panel-exp-to-log" class="exp-panel hidden space-y-5">
        <div class="border-b border-slate-200/80 pb-3 dark:border-slate-800">
          <h2 class="text-base sm:text-lg font-black tracking-tight text-slate-900 dark:text-white flex items-center gap-2">
            <span>⚡</span> Convert Exponential Expression to Logarithmic Form
          </h2>
          <p class="mt-1 text-xs text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400">
            Apply the inverse relationship <strong class="font-mono">bᵃ = c ⟺ log_b(c) = a</strong>.
          </p>
        </div>

        <form id="form-exp" class="space-y-4" novalidate onsubmit="return false;">
          <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-3 gap-4">
            
            <!-- Base (b) -->
            <div>
              <div class="flex items-center justify-between">
                <label for="input-exp-base" class="block text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300">
                  Base (b)
                </label>
                <button type="button" id="btn-use-e-exp" class="text-[11px] font-bold text-blue-600 hover:underline dark:text-blue-400 cursor-pointer">
                  Use Natural e
                </button>
              </div>
              <input
                type="text"
                id="input-exp-base"
                value=""
                placeholder="e.g. 2, 3, 10, or e"
                class="mt-1.5 w-full rounded-xl border border-slate-300 bg-white p-3 text-base font-bold text-slate-900 shadow-2xs focus:border-blue-600 focus:outline-hidden dark:border-slate-700 dark:bg-slate-900 dark:text-white"
              />
              <span class="text-[11px] text-slate-500 mt-1 block">b &gt; 0 and b ≠ 1</span>
            </div>

            <!-- Exponent (a) -->
            <div>
              <label for="input-exp-power" class="block text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300">
                Exponent / Power (a)
              </label>
              <input
                type="number"
                id="input-exp-power"
                value=""
                step="any"
                placeholder="e.g. 5, 4, -2"
                class="mt-1.5 w-full rounded-xl border border-slate-300 bg-white p-3 text-base font-bold text-slate-900 shadow-2xs focus:border-blue-600 focus:outline-hidden dark:border-slate-700 dark:bg-slate-900 dark:text-white"
              />
              <span class="text-[11px] text-slate-500 mt-1 block">Any real power</span>
            </div>

            <!-- Evaluated Result (c) -->
            <div>
              <label for="input-exp-result" class="block text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300">
                Evaluated Result (c)
              </label>
              <input
                type="number"
                id="input-exp-result"
                value=""
                step="any"
                placeholder="Optional (auto-computed)"
                class="mt-1.5 w-full rounded-xl border border-slate-300 bg-white p-3 text-base font-bold text-slate-900 shadow-2xs focus:border-blue-600 focus:outline-hidden dark:border-slate-700 dark:bg-slate-900 dark:text-white"
              />
              <span class="text-[11px] text-slate-500 mt-1 block">Auto-calculated if empty</span>
            </div>

          </div>

          <div class="flex items-center gap-2 pt-1">
            <button
              type="submit"
              id="btn-calc-exp"
              class="flex-1 rounded-xl bg-blue-600 hover:bg-blue-700 px-6 py-3 text-sm font-extrabold text-white shadow-lg shadow-blue-600/25 transition active:scale-[0.98] cursor-pointer"
            >
              Convert to Logarithmic Form →
            </button>
            <button
              type="button"
              id="btn-clear-exp"
              class="rounded-xl border border-slate-300 bg-white px-4 py-3 text-sm font-bold text-slate-700 hover:bg-slate-100 dark:border-slate-700 dark:bg-slate-800 dark:text-slate-200 transition cursor-pointer"
            >
              Clear
            </button>
          </div>

          <p id="err-exp" class="hidden rounded-xl border border-red-200 bg-red-50 p-3 text-xs font-semibold text-red-700 dark:border-red-900/60 dark:bg-red-950/30 dark:text-red-300" role="alert" aria-live="polite"></p>

          <!-- Result Card -->
          <div id="res-exp-card" class="hidden space-y-4 rounded-3xl border border-blue-200 bg-white p-5 dark:border-blue-900/60 dark:bg-slate-900">
            <div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row sm:items-center sm:justify-between gap-3 border-b border-slate-200 pb-4 dark:border-slate-800">
              <div>
                <span class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-blue-700 dark:text-blue-400">Equivalent Logarithmic Form</span>
                <div id="res-exp-log" class="mt-1 text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-black text-blue-600 dark:text-blue-400 font-mono">log₂(32) = 5</div>
              </div>
              <div class="sm:text-right">
                <span class="text-xs font-bold text-slate-500 uppercase tracking-wider">Input Exponential Form:</span>
                <div id="res-exp-in" class="text-sm sm:text-base font-bold text-slate-800 dark:text-slate-200 font-mono">2⁵ = 32</div>
              </div>
            </div>

            <details class="group rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 bg-slate-50 p-4 dark:border-slate-800 dark:bg-slate-950" open>
              <summary class="cursor-pointer list-none flex items-center justify-between text-xs font-bold text-slate-800 dark:text-slate-200">
                <span>📝 Step-by-Step Conversion Derivation</span>
                <span class="text-blue-600 dark:text-blue-400 group-open:rotate-180 transition-transform">▼</span>
              </summary>
              <ul id="res-exp-steps" class="mt-3 space-y-1.5 text-xs text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300 list-disc list-inside font-mono leading-relaxed"></ul>
            </details>
          </div>
        </form>
      </div>

    </div>

  </div>

  <!-- EDUCATIONAL CONTENT SLOT -->
  <Fragment slot="content">
    <section class="exponential-content space-y-6">

      <div>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">What Is Exponential Form?</h2>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300">
          In mathematics, <strong>exponential form</strong> is a concise notation for expressing repeated multiplication using two primary elements: a <strong>base</strong> and an <strong>exponent</strong> (or power). Instead of writing a number as a lengthy product of repeated factors, exponents indicate exactly how many times the base is multiplied by itself.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300">
          When dealing with positive whole numbers, exponential form is derived directly from the number's <strong>prime factorization</strong>. By decomposing a composite integer into its indivisible prime building blocks and grouping duplicate factors, the number is expressed in its unique exponential signature. For instance, consider the number 250:
        </p>
        <div class="my-3 rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 bg-slate-100/80 p-4 font-mono text-sm font-semibold text-slate-900 dark:border-slate-800 dark:bg-slate-900 dark:text-white">
          250 = 2 × 5 × 5 × 5 = 2 × 5³
        </div>
        <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300">
          Here, 2 is multiplied once and 5 is multiplied three times. Rather than writing three individual fives, the exponential notation <code>5³</code> compactly represents this repeated multiplication.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">Exponential Form vs. Exponential (Scientific) Notation</h2>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300">
          It is essential to distinguish between <strong>prime-factor exponential form</strong> and <strong>scientific/exponential notation</strong>, as these mathematical terms are frequently confused:
        </p>
        <div class="mt-3 overflow-x-auto">
          <table class="w-full text-left text-xs border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800 rounded-xl overflow-hidden">
            <thead class="bg-slate-100 dark:bg-slate-900 text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300">
              <tr>
                <th class="p-3">Concept</th>
                <th class="p-3">Primary Purpose</th>
                <th class="p-3">Permitted Inputs</th>
                <th class="p-3">Example</th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody class="divide-y divide-slate-200 dark:divide-slate-800 text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400">
              <tr>
                <td class="p-3 font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">Prime-Factor Exponential Form</td>
                <td class="p-3">Decomposes integers into prime factor powers</td>
                <td class="p-3">Positive whole numbers (integers &gt; 0)</td>
                <td class="p-3 font-mono">128 = 2⁷<br/>360 = 2³ × 3² × 5</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td class="p-3 font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">Scientific / Exponential Notation</td>
                <td class="p-3">Expresses very large or tiny quantities using powers of 10</td>
                <td class="p-3">Any real number including decimals and fractions</td>
                <td class="p-3 font-mono">24.65 = 2.465 × 10¹<br/>0.0042 = 4.2 × 10⁻³</td>
              </tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
        <p class="mt-2 text-xs text-slate-500 italic">
          This calculator primarily focuses on <strong>prime-factor exponential form</strong> for positive integers and the <strong>algebraic conversion between logarithmic and exponential equations</strong>.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">How to Write a Whole Number in Exponential Form</h2>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300">
          Transforming any positive integer into exponential form involves a systematic five-step prime factorization procedure:
        </p>
        <ol class="mt-3 space-y-2 text-sm text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300 list-decimal list-inside leading-relaxed">
          <li><strong>Start with a positive whole number:</strong> Ensure the number is an integer strictly greater than zero.</li>
          <li><strong>Find its prime factorization:</strong> Divide the number successively by the smallest prime divisors (2, 3, 5, 7, 11, etc.) until the quotient reaches 1.</li>
          <li><strong>Group identical prime factors:</strong> Collect every repetition of the same prime number into a single group.</li>
          <li><strong>Count occurrences:</strong> Tally how many times each prime factor divides into the original number.</li>
          <li><strong>Assign exponents:</strong> Write each unique prime factor as a base, with its frequency count as the superscript exponent. If a factor occurs only once, the exponent of 1 is omitted by convention.</li>
        </ol>

        <div class="mt-4 rounded-2xl border border-blue-200 bg-blue-50/50 p-4 dark:border-blue-900/50 dark:bg-blue-950/30">
          <span class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-blue-700 dark:text-blue-300 block mb-1">Detailed Walkthrough: Number 72</span>
          <div class="text-xs font-mono text-slate-800 dark:text-slate-200 space-y-1">
            <p>72 ÷ 2 = 36</p>
            <p>36 ÷ 2 = 18</p>
            <p>18 ÷ 2 = 9</p>
            <p>9 ÷ 3 = 3</p>
            <p>3 ÷ 3 = 1</p>
            <p class="pt-1 font-bold text-blue-600 dark:text-blue-400">Prime Factorization: 72 = 2 × 2 × 2 × 3 × 3</p>
            <p class="font-bold text-emerald-600 dark:text-emerald-400">Exponential Form: 72 = 2³ × 3²</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">Logarithmic to Exponential Conversion</h2>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300">
          Logarithms and exponents are mathematical inverse operations of each other. A logarithm answers the question: <em>"To what power must I raise base b to obtain value c?"</em>
        </p>
        <div class="my-3 rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 bg-slate-100/80 p-4 font-mono text-sm font-semibold text-slate-900 dark:border-slate-800 dark:bg-slate-900 dark:text-white text-center">
          log<sub>b</sub>(c) = a &nbsp;&nbsp;⟺&nbsp;&nbsp; b<sup>a</sup> = c
        </div>
        <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300">
          To convert any logarithmic equation into an exponential equation:
        </p>
        <ul class="mt-2 space-y-1.5 text-sm text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300 list-disc list-inside">
          <li>The subscript base of the logarithm (<code class="font-mono">b</code>) becomes the base of the power.</li>
          <li>The isolated logarithm value (<code class="font-mono">a</code>) becomes the exponent.</li>
          <li>The argument inside the logarithm (<code class="font-mono">c</code>) becomes the evaluated result.</li>
        </ul>
        <div class="my-3 rounded-xl border border-slate-200 bg-slate-50 p-3 text-xs font-mono text-slate-800 dark:border-slate-800 dark:bg-slate-900 dark:text-slate-200">
          Example: log₂(8) = 3 &nbsp;⟹&nbsp; 2³ = 8
        </div>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">Natural Logarithms and Euler's Number ($e$)</h2>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300">
          When the base of a logarithm is Euler's constant <code class="font-mono">e ≈ 2.718281828...</code>, the expression is called a <strong>natural logarithm</strong> and is written as <code class="font-mono">ln(c)</code> instead of <code class="font-mono">log_e(c)</code>.
        </p>
        <div class="my-3 rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 bg-slate-100/80 p-4 font-mono text-sm font-semibold text-slate-900 dark:border-slate-800 dark:bg-slate-900 dark:text-white text-center">
          ln(c) = a &nbsp;&nbsp;⟺&nbsp;&nbsp; e<sup>a</sup> = c
        </div>
        <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300">
          For instance, <code class="font-mono">ln(15) ≈ 2.70805</code> is equivalent to the exponential form <code class="font-mono">e²·⁷⁰⁸⁰⁵ ≈ 15</code>.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">Exponential to Logarithmic Conversion</h2>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300">
          The reverse conversion transforms an exponential equation into its equivalent logarithmic format:
        </p>
        <div class="my-3 rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 bg-slate-100/80 p-4 font-mono text-sm font-semibold text-slate-900 dark:border-slate-800 dark:bg-slate-900 dark:text-white text-center">
          b<sup>a</sup> = c &nbsp;&nbsp;⟺&nbsp;&nbsp; log<sub>b</sub>(c) = a
        </div>
        <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300">
          For example:
        </p>
        <ul class="mt-2 space-y-1 text-xs font-mono text-slate-800 dark:text-slate-200 list-disc list-inside">
          <li>2⁵ = 32 &nbsp;⟹&nbsp; log₂(32) = 5</li>
          <li>3⁴ = 81 &nbsp;⟹&nbsp; log₃(81) = 4</li>
          <li>10³ = 1000 &nbsp;⟹&nbsp; log₁₀(1000) = 3 (Common Logarithm)</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">Special Mathematical Cases: Primes, Zero, and Negatives</h2>
        <div class="space-y-3 mt-3 text-sm text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300 leading-relaxed">
          <p>
            <strong>Prime Numbers:</strong> By definition, a prime number has exactly two positive factors: 1 and itself. Consequently, when a prime number such as 13, 17, or 31 is factored, its prime factorization is simply the number itself raised to the first power (e.g. <code>13 = 13</code> or <code>13¹</code>).
          </p>
          <p>
            <strong>Zero and Negative Integers:</strong> Prime factorization applies strictly to positive integers ($n \ge 2$). Zero cannot be factored into primes because multiplying by zero annihilates other factors ($0 = 0 \times p$). Negative numbers are excluded from classical prime factorization because prime numbers are defined as positive integers greater than 1.
          </p>
          <p>
            <strong>Logarithm Base Restrictions:</strong> In real analysis, a logarithm base must satisfy <code class="font-mono">b &gt; 0</code> and <code class="font-mono">b ≠ 1</code>. If $b = 1$, then $1^a = 1$ for all real $a$, meaning $\log_1(c)$ cannot produce any unique solution. Furthermore, negative bases lead to non-real complex numbers when evaluated at fractional powers.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">Worked Examples Reference Table</h2>
        <div class="overflow-x-auto my-3">
          <table class="w-full text-left text-xs border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800 rounded-xl overflow-hidden">
